content:
The evidence is now clear enough. All failing orders have invoices from "Al-Noor Trading" and all appeared after t=671 (3 s after the worker v1.0.2 deploy at t=668). The messages were created starting t=671 and are all stuck retrying. No competing explanation is supported — the payment-service deploy at t=442 is 229 s before the first anomaly and no payment invariants are violated (E2). The root cause is the worker bad deploy.

```json
{
  "investigate": [],
  "hypotheses": [
    {
      "service": "worker",
      "kind": "bad_deploy",
      "mechanism": "Worker v1.0.2 (deployed t=668, 3 s before first anomaly) introduced a regression in invoice extraction that cannot parse the layout used by Al-Noor Trading invoices, causing every affected message to retry until the 5-attempt budget is exhausted.",
      "supporting": ["E1", "E3", "E4", "E6", "E13", "E14"],
      "refuting": [],
      "explains": ["I6_retry_budget"],
      "repair_plan": [
        {"action": "rollback_service", "params": {"service": "worker"}},
        {"action": "requeue_orphaned_orders", "params": {}}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Worker v1.0.2 deployed at t=668 broke invoice extraction for Al-Noor Trading invoices, causing 5+ messages to exhaust their retry budgets; rolling back the worker and re-queuing the stranded orders will resolve the incident."
}
```
